# The inline prune in ForgetAsync stops accounting the tombstones it retires
# into the retirement epoch, so a batch prune lowers the composite revision.
MODULE: AtomicCommit
ROW: RevisionMonotonic
FILE: src/lattice/BPlusTree/Grains/TxRegistryGrain.cs
DETECTORS: TxRegistryGrainTests.GetDecisionsRevisionAsync_never_decreases_across_a_batch_prune
SUMMARY: a batch prune of expired tombstones is not compensated, so the revision token falls

--- FIND
        var retired = pruned.Tombstones?.Count ?? 0;
        state.State.TombstoneRetirementEpoch += retired;
--- REPLACE
        var retired = pruned.Tombstones?.Count ?? 0;
--- END